{"author":{"id":"a3a282966ced55effb4560271fcd98e13241af24ea76b00ec76a0f18154bc8ee"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790975007,"nonce":"caWPNaXPxA5wsUknhJFlnxLSy+8=","title":"issue get and the list take --at TIME; issue log takes --from/--to and a PROGRAM","message":"The snapshot primitive and the log window. `--at TIME` replays an issue's operations whose own wall-clock time is at or before TIME with the issue package's apply rules and returns the ordinary snapshot or excerpt; the list runs its program over the excerpts as they stood then, archived-at-the-time excluded as today. `--from`/`--to` on the log select operations in [from, to); the log takes one ID or the list's PROGRAM and returns the selected issues' operations. TIME forms: a date, an RFC 3339 time, a duration (7d). Mirrored one to one in Starlark.","files":null,"fields":{"area":["cli","issue-model"],"parent":"58e95ffebf5125dca645530ce3c87dd1dc42fd3124eb70e08f4bc48ce27b15e2","priority":"high","status":"in-progress","type":"task"}}]}